 "safe_design_checklist": {
  "1_pins": "PASS: every data pin registered in RTL on the root of the band at its face (W rin / E rout glue on c; bin / bout / gin / straps / attn on t (n); xi_* entry on t (s); S-face xo_* / gout / straps on c); rout = new glue pin register (+1) instead of the hard row_e flop (internal insertion 104-119 TT); reset captured beside its pin on that band root (u_lpr_pin, uniform +1); band clock pins enter their own band.",
  "2_reach": "every registered hop inside one band (<= ~410 um tall bands); every seam a landing (E=2 multicycle ring -> read, <= ~750 um over 2 cycles): t->c xb / gin / strap landings span the x-store band (411-600 um); the reset pin stage -> lp root hop is 1 bit (<= ~710 um, repeated); actual route timing decides.",
  "3_fanout": "r3 / r5 kept copies unchanged; landings chunked 24 b with the r5 per-slot reset copies (ot_rp5_land_reset_split.sv); every scalar reset pad on its own forest leaf; pre-gate native census decides.",
  "4_depth": "PASS: cut only at existing register stages / landings (registered slot mux); no new combinational path.",
  "5_storage": "PASS: unchanged hard SRAM children (x store, PV merge, columns); landing rings D=4 slots of flops.",
  "6_floorplan": "r5 outline 691.2 x 1252.8 and child placement unchanged; bands u y712.8-1123.2, t y1123.2-1252.8, c y0-712.8; +27774 landing flops; per-band utilisation printed by the fence hook (R6_FENCE ... util, error > 0.85).",
  "7_clock": "3 GEOMETRIC band roots (ck_u, ck_t, ck_c), each a fenced band <= 691 x 412 um (x-store band root without IO = all-internal scope); every band seam landed (lp audit PASS, 10 landings), 1-bit reset runs only; judged per root at the pin flops TT+FF <= 80.",
  "8_schedule": "static; every landed net +3 absorbed in removed relays / pads where possible; vs r3: gout +5 (r5 5), rout +1 (glue), bout 0, half reset +1 uniform; consumer reset depths shifted with their data. PRICED: rp4a gout G 10 -> 15 per SM tile hop, rout +1 per half."
 },
